WEBVTT

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:05.420
Then I'll be the one to stop you.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:07.630
Just try to stop me.

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:10.050
Let's settle the score.

00:00:56.510 --> 00:01:01.600
You can predict your opponent's movements?
What a clever move.

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:05.730
It's not like I can do it with anyone.
It's only because it's you.

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:06.440
What?

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:09.360
You're the same as me.
That's why I can tell.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:16.160
I am not you.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:17.530
You are me!

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:23.080
That power of yours must work well
against the Dead End.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:24.290
However...

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:30.920
My evolution is a power that's only meant... to kill!

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:40.180
You sought salvation. I sought death.

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:44.230
That's the difference between us!

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:59.660
It looks like it's begun...

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:38.470
Encounter: Our Future

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:51.600
So you've run away.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:54.560
I can hear both of their emotions.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:58.900
Just like their two hearts,
a beautiful coda.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:03.820
The final battle...

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:04.660
Yeah.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:20.970
If you want to fight, I can take you on.

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:27.930
You're a feisty little boy.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:33.270
Looks like things are getting interesting.

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:36.400
O-Olga...

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.400
Wh-What should we do?

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.070
What should we do, you say?

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:43.240
Excuse me, everyone...

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.030
<i>Both sides, retreat!</i>

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:48.700
You idiots! Don't fight just because it feels like what you're supposed to do!

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:53.580
If you want to fight even after you've lost your reason to do so, come to me!

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:56.790
I'll fight as much as you want!

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:03.340
What an old geezer.

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:09.640
Our nemesis the Timekeepers have fallen.

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:12.640
I wouldn't like to see any more humans dying.

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:15.980
I'll agree to that.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:20.440
Then are you going to leave those two alone?

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:22.860
I don't care whether you do or not.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:25.610
<i>I do believe in Lord Tohru.</i>

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:29.620
<i>It's only fitting that
we entrust the future to the young ones.</i>

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:34.500
Exactly. Hey, you guys,
we'll entrust the battle to those two.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.500
That's fine, right?

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:35.930
Yup.

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:36.210
Yes.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:37.210
- Yeah!
- Yes.

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:37.900
Well, yeah.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:38.630
Right.

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:39.590
That's fine.

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:40.590
- Good with me.
- Yeah.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:43.210
All right, it's a unanimous decision!

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:45.430
No grudges held,
no matter which side wins!

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:46.550
<i>I'll hold a grudge!</i>

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:48.800
Don't force everything onto Tohru!

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:51.060
There's no way I can
just leave Tohru alone like that!

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:52.140
- Stupid Big Brother!
- Stupid Big Brother!

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:58.100
Do whatever you want...

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:09.620
This is—

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:23.210
This must be our destiny.
It's the same place we were before.

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:26.130
It's not the same!

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:30.470
Your gun handling has gotten decent, huh?

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:35.930
You're that strong, but you still seek power?

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:38.900
Of course!  I need it to change the world!

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:42.360
That's too dangerous.
That's the power that creates the Dead End!

00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:44.530
Because it's dangerous,
it needs to be controlled.

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:46.280
I'll make that happen!

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:49.160
That's arrogance!
What would happen if you were to die?

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:50.820
It'll be fine as long as I don't die.

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:53.700
That train of thought
is what creates the Dead End!

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:59.000
You're just going to cower from danger
and disregard all the possibilities?

00:06:59.170 --> 00:06:59.830
That's not it!

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.670
What's wrong with wishing for evolution?

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:05.800
Is living naked inside a cave your ideal?

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:06.840
That's not it!

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:10.640
If you want to change the world,
just change it one day at a time.

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:13.810
You should be able to evolve,
even without powers like that!

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:19.600
You're telling me to wait...

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:20.730
That's right, I am!

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:24.360
Even if things don't change this second,
we can change the future a little bit at a time.

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:26.570
If we do, someday—

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:27.940
Shut up!

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:37.450
Remy died!

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:41.000
Even now, children are starving,
getting sick, and dying!

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:43.840
You're telling me to just sit and watch that happen?

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:45.250
That's not what I mean...

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:47.380
You guys are living in wealth!

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:50.380
You guys can afford
to wait decades and centuries!

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:51.590
But still—

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:53.300
However, that's not the case for us!

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:56.390
But still... that's better than everything
turning into dust and disappearing!

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:57.640
You coward!

00:07:57.640 --> 00:07:58.810
You stubborn fool!

00:08:03.190 --> 00:08:04.730
What would you know?

00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:08.570
If you don't have power,
you can't save anyone at all!

00:08:20.710 --> 00:08:22.620
I will protect Tohru!

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:25.790
Tohru isn't the type of man
that needs someone to protect him!

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:27.840
Our Tohru is very kind!

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:31.380
Maybe you're overprotective
and making him indecisive?

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:35.430
What do you know about Tohru?

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:39.600
Tohru's strong!
That's why I fight together with him!

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:57.450
<i>His feelings and his courage...</i>

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:59.700
<i>By trading blows, they enter into me.</i>

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:06.630
<i>He's just like me.
He has things he wants to protect, too.</i>

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:09.670
<i>You might handle it well...</i>

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:11.800
<i>But we...</i>

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:16.180
<i>We can't hand over our future
to anyone else!</i>

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:29.980
In order to survive,
I have to believe in myself.

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:33.070
Tohru!

00:10:28.170 --> 00:10:29.380
Kyoka...

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:34.670
Shields activated.

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:36.090
Shields activated.

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:37.800
Shields activated.

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:52.230
Tohru.

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:54.250
I told you, this time we're enemies.

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:55.030
Drop your gun.

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:00.320
Kyoka, shoot!

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:05.120
Shoot!

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:07.660
Shoot!

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:13.250
Tohru!

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:22.800
Don't you hate me?

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:25.180
I do hate you.

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:28.310
You're the one that took Sidune.

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:30.270
Then shoot.

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:31.560
Never.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:33.900
If you don't shoot, the war will continue.

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:37.570
Hating each another...
killing each other, what does that create?

00:11:38.150 --> 00:11:39.080
I'm going to end it all.

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:40.030
Stop it...

00:11:40.410 --> 00:11:43.120
Both killing and being killed.

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:47.120
Without it, you can't return to the future either!

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:48.620
So what?

00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:03.180
He really did it.

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:07.060
The chrono-potential is rapidly changing.

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:09.730
Wh-What in the world is going on?

00:12:09.730 --> 00:12:13.810
This is... The two histories
are separating from each other!

00:12:14.690 --> 00:12:17.070
Oh, this is beautiful.

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:23.160
It's the end already? How boring.

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:27.540
Everything is fading away, I see.

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:32.330
Now, where we end up...
will it be our world, or will it be Hell?

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:35.590
Can you not hear it?

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:40.920
This beautiful madrigal...
what a majestic calando!

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:43.640
Is this the end of it all?

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:46.260
No, this is where it begins.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:49.020
Hold on, what in the world is this?

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:51.560
Fretting won't get you anywhere.

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:56.110
Jonathan, you...

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:03.740
Matsurika!

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:09.660
Listen! That guy there...
don't you ever let him go!

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:13.830
I-I know that!

00:13:22.380 --> 00:13:24.800
'Til the very end,
he was an infuriating bastard.

00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:29.760
As much as you can...

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:44.110
I wonder if we did the right thing.

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:46.450
I don't know.

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:49.530
But since you were here with me,
I was able to make it this far.

00:13:50.490 --> 00:13:53.370
Yup. We'll be together forever, right?

00:13:58.840 --> 00:13:59.670
Kyoka...

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:00.920
Tohru...

00:14:26.450 --> 00:14:29.320
"We'll see each other again..."
I did say that, right?

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:33.660
Yeah.

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:43.130
Were we able to change the future?

00:14:43.510 --> 00:14:48.680
Yes. My future was supposed to have been
completely swallowed up by the Dead End.

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:51.390
Tohru, you changed the future.

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:52.970
That's a relief.

00:14:53.930 --> 00:14:56.480
It is... right?

00:14:56.640 --> 00:14:57.770
Is something wrong?

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:02.730
Thanks to you, Tohru,
my future has been saved.

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:06.400
But that was a selfish wish I had made.

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:12.330
Perhaps there might have been a different path...
a better path.

00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:16.870
If you weren't around, we would've
only had the future with the Dead End.

00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:21.750
But, for instance,
if you had used that Energy Cube,

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:24.920
you might have been able
to create a real time machine.

00:15:25.510 --> 00:15:28.590
Tohru, you might have been able
to see your parents that way, too...

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:32.350
A real time machine, huh?

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:39.730
Memories are important,
but Dad and Mom gave me the future.

00:15:40.440 --> 00:15:43.610
That's why I need to move forward.

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:48.150
This is goodbye, then?

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:52.370
Yeah, thank you for everything until now.

00:15:52.370 --> 00:15:54.280
No, I should be the one...

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:56.790
Will we see each other again?

00:15:57.500 --> 00:16:02.380
Yes. If you are moving forward to the future,
Tohru, I'm sure we will.

00:16:02.380 --> 00:16:03.420
I'm glad.

00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:09.420
Oh, right.

00:16:11.890 --> 00:16:15.140
I've been meaning to ask you...
what's your name?

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:18.980
Actually... I don't remember.

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:23.980
I lost many things
when I came back to the past.

00:16:24.310 --> 00:16:29.360
I see, then what should I call you
the next time I see you?

00:16:29.690 --> 00:16:33.660
If you don't mind...
Tohru, come up with something for me.

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:35.740
A name for you?

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:40.000
Miki...

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:44.210
How about using the character for "future"
and reading it as "miki"?

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:49.460
Because you were far ahead of me
and showed me infinite possibilities...

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:51.260
Miki...

00:16:54.390 --> 00:16:55.970
Thank you very much.

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:01.770
I'll see you again, Miki.

00:17:02.140 --> 00:17:04.440
Yes. I'll see you again.

00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:15.910
<i>The strange disease where human bodies
disappear like sand...</i>

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:19.660
<i>Does the Desert Syndrome really exist?</i>

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:22.910
<i>Or is it merely a hallucinogen attack created by
terrorists fighting against the regime?</i>

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:25.250
<i>The truth will be revealed right after this!</i>

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:28.420
<i>I don't dislike my school uniform.</i>

00:17:29.460 --> 00:17:31.420
<i>It's not unpleasant
to have lots of comrades.</i>

00:17:33.090 --> 00:17:36.680
<i>Though we wear the same clothes,
who we are inside varies.</i>

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:41.270
<i>And, despite the differences,
we all walk the same paths together.</i>

00:17:48.190 --> 00:17:49.570
<i>We're all on the same planet...</i>

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:52.570
<i>...and we walk towards the same future.</i>

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:53.860
Tohru!

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:55.700
Morning!

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:57.570
Morning, Kyoka.

00:17:58.490 --> 00:18:00.540
<i>We returned back here.</i>

00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:04.040
<i>It feels like we made quite a long detour.</i>

00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:11.420
Damn you, Tohru, you bast—

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:14.720
Stupid Big Brother.

00:18:15.050 --> 00:18:16.300
Let's go, Tohru.

00:18:17.050 --> 00:18:18.090
Sure.

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:21.770
<i>Our everyday life basically went back
to what it used to be.</i>

00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:25.350
What?

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:27.020
A love triangle?

00:18:28.060 --> 00:18:29.110
What's wrong?

00:18:29.900 --> 00:18:31.820
Nothing. Let's go.

00:18:56.760 --> 00:18:59.090
Are you thinking about the Degradation?

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:01.970
You could tell, huh?

00:19:02.970 --> 00:19:06.390
According to Big Brother,
there are a lot fewer cases now, you know?

00:19:06.770 --> 00:19:11.730
That means that the future where the Dead End is created
isn't completely gone yet, I guess.

00:19:11.980 --> 00:19:17.170
<b>“What then is time?
If no one asks me, 
I know what it is. 
If I wish to explain it to him 
who asks, I do not know."</b>

00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:15.900
We have to do something about it,
a little bit at a time.

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:17.200
Right.

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:24.450
Then let's get married!

00:19:24.990 --> 00:19:27.080
You're going to try
to become the president, right?

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:28.160
Y-Yeah.

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:32.840
Then marry me, shove Big Brother aside
and take control of the Katagiri Group!

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.210
You can leave all
the information warfare to Kumi,

00:19:35.210 --> 00:19:39.430
and you can contact Ms. Olga and 
Aaron to expand your forces.

00:19:39.430 --> 00:19:42.140
You can conquer Eurasia
within seven years, and then—

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:46.020
Kyoka, that's not being the president of the 
world, that's world domination!

00:19:46.020 --> 00:19:47.350
Close enough!

00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:52.980
How about a future like that?

00:19:55.530 --> 00:19:56.940
Yeah, sounds good.

00:19:56.940 --> 00:19:57.900
Tohru!

00:19:58.860 --> 00:20:01.450
<i>Did the future really change?</i>

00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:04.410
<i>Or will it change from here on?</i>

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:07.620
Hi! It's been a while.

00:20:08.460 --> 00:20:10.540
Really? Yes...

00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:14.290
I'm pretty expensive, you know?

00:20:16.130 --> 00:20:18.420
<i>In the end, what is time?</i>

00:20:18.720 --> 00:20:20.510
<i>I still don't know.</i>

00:20:21.430 --> 00:20:24.510
<i>Even if we don't know, we move forward.</i>

00:20:25.350 --> 00:20:28.060
<i>One day at a time, then one more day at a time.</i>

00:20:29.310 --> 00:20:32.150
<i>It may not be a very simple path,</i>

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:34.440
<i>but no matter how hard it is,</i>

00:20:35.480 --> 00:20:37.730
<i>if you're together with me,
I can keep walking on.</i>

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:43.070
<i>Believing that someday,
I will meet that girl at the far end of the path...</i>

00:20:47.910 --> 00:20:48.870
Here goes!

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:50.000
Bring it!

00:20:51.120 --> 00:20:53.000
Oh, sorry!

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:55.380
Where were you throwing that?

00:20:54.540 --> 00:20:56.750
<b>Memorial of Peace
Gifted by the First President of the World</b>

00:20:59.550 --> 00:21:00.970
Excuse me!

00:21:02.130 --> 00:21:04.090
Thank you very much!

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:12.690
Miki.

00:21:24.530 --> 00:21:26.990
Grandpa!

00:21:38.090 --> 00:21:39.120
Shall we go?

00:21:39.120 --> 00:21:39.590
Yeah!

00:21:48.180 --> 00:21:49.680
You know, Miki...

00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:51.770
What is it?

00:21:52.560 --> 00:21:54.770
We got to meet again, didn't we?

00:22:00.530 --> 00:22:01.820
Hey!

00:22:02.240 --> 00:22:03.450
Sorry!
